    <summary>Shell history for PowerShell: every command with where and when it ran, found again with Ctrl+R.</summary>
    <description>
hit records every command you run in PowerShell, with the directory it ran in, when, how long it took and whether it failed, and finds it again with a fuzzy finder on Ctrl+R.

Highlights:
* Ctrl+R opens the finder seeded with what you have typed; Enter puts the command back at the prompt, multi-line commands intact.
* Scopes: everything, this machine, this session, or just this folder (Alt+D).
* Sort by rank or by most recent (Alt+S); a leading ' matches literally.
* Groups defined in config.toml (git, devops, …), marked in the list and picked with Alt+G then a letter.
* Ctrl+Y copies a command to the clipboard; Del removes it from history.
* Plain JSON Lines storage you own; nothing leaves your machine.

Setup after install - add this line to your PowerShell profile ($PROFILE):

    Invoke-Expression (&amp; hit init pwsh | Out-String)

Then open a new shell and press Ctrl+R. The package does not edit your profile.
    </description>
